  - cmds:
      - view 1
    text: |
      {[ht,$start]&thinsp;Space, Time, and Energy}

      SW developers conventionally characterize their pro&shy;grams in terms of _time_ versus _space_ &ndash; a classic trade-off.

      But when targeting HW with limited power sources, we must also measure our programs&rsquo; _energy_ consumption.

      Consider `SleepyRunnerP`&thinsp;{[tr,102/07/03]} as a case in point:

      {[DC,1]} **EM&bull;Builder** itself reports code&thinsp;&middot;&thinsp;data size [bytes]<br>
      {[DC,2]} **Logic 2** measures execution time [&mu;s] {[tr,102/08/02]}<br>
      {[DC,3]} **Joulescope Viewer** show power [mW] over time [&mu;J]

      Note how {[dc,2]} and {[dc,3]} reveal complementary perspectives on the _same_ burst of active work.

      <div class="em-info">

      The next tour will formally introduce [Joulescope](https://www.joulescope.com/).

      </div>

